# Intuition

To find the intersection of two arrays, we need to find the elements that are present in both arrays.

I first sort both arrays. Once they are sorted, I can use two pointers to compare the elements efficiently.

If the current elements are equal, that element belongs to the intersection. Since the answer should contain only unique elements, I check whether the last added element is different before adding it.

If `nums1[i]` is smaller, I move `i` forward because that element cannot match the current `nums2[j]`.

If `nums2[j]` is smaller, I move `j` forward for the same reason.

# Approach

1. Sort both `nums1` and `nums2`.
2. Initialize two pointers:
   - `i` for `nums1`
   - `j` for `nums2`
3. Compare `nums1[i]` and `nums2[j]`:
   - If they are equal, add the element to the answer if it is not already present, then increment both pointers.
   - If `nums1[i] < nums2[j]`, increment `i`.
   - Otherwise, increment `j`.
4. Continue until either pointer reaches the end of its array.
5. Convert the `ArrayList` into an integer array and return it.

# Complexity

- Time complexity: O(n log n + m log m)
- Space complexity: O(n + m)

The sorting takes `O(n log n + m log m)`, and the two-pointer traversal takes `O(n + m)`.

The `ArrayList` and returned array together require `O(n + m)` space in the worst case.

# Code

```java
class Solution {

    public int[] intersection(int[] nums1, int[] nums2) {

        int n = nums1.length;
        int m = nums2.length;

        Arrays.sort(nums1);
        Arrays.sort(nums2);

        ArrayList<Integer> ans = new ArrayList<>();

        int i = 0;
        int j = 0;

        while (i < n && j < m) {

            if (nums1[i] == nums2[j]) {

                if (ans.size() == 0 ||
                    ans.get(ans.size() - 1) != nums1[i]) {

                    ans.add(nums1[i]);
                }

                i++;
                j++;
            }
            else if (nums1[i] < nums2[j]) {
                i++;
            }
            else {
                j++;
            }
        }

        int arr[] = new int[ans.size()];

        for (int k = 0; k < ans.size(); k++) {
            arr[k] = ans.get(k);
        }

        return arr;
    }
}
